                "event": "Frost Advisory",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Portland OR",
                "headline": "Frost Advisory issued October 30 at 10:13PM PDT until October 31 at 9:00AM PDT by NWS Portland OR",
                "description": "* WHAT...Temperatures of 36 degrees or lower will result in frost\nformation.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of northwest and west central Oregon and southwest\nWashington.\n\n* WHEN...Until 9 AM PDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Frost could harm sensitive outdoor vegetation. Sensitive\noutdoor plants may be killed if left uncovered.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...There is a 20-30% chance that temperatures\nwill fall below 32 degrees, especially for locations that do not\ndevelop fog. Frost and freeze headlines are only issued through the\ngrowing season of April 1 through October 31. Therefore, frost or\nfreeze headlines will not be issued beginning November 1, even\nthough similar low temperatures are possible. Frost and freeze\nheadlines will no longer be issued this growing season for the\nUpper Hood River Valley, southern Willamette Valley, south\nWashington Cascade Foothills, and north Oregon Coast Range as these\nlocations have already experienced a hard freeze earlier in\nOctober.",
                "instruction": "Take steps now to protect tender outdoor plants from the cold.\nConsider temporarily moving outdoor potted plants indoors if they are\nsensitive to cold temperatures.\n\nConsider temporarily covering sensitive plants with a lightweight\ncotton fabric (i.e., bedsheets, thin blankets), as this will help\nretain heat and provide frost protection for your plants.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "NPWPQR"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WWUS76 KPQR 310513"
