                "senderName": "NWS Seattle WA",
                "headline": "Freeze Warning issued October 30 at 5:43PM PDT until October 31 at 9:00AM PDT by NWS Seattle WA",
                "description": "* WHAT...Sub-freezing temperatures around 29 to 32 expected.\nTemperatures may vary due to clearing or fog development in\nlocalized areas.\n\n* WHERE...Middle Chehalis River Valley and Lowlands of Lewis and\nSouthern Thurston Counties.\n\n* WHEN...From midnight tonight to 9 AM PDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Frost and freeze conditions could kill crops, other\nsensitive vegetation and possibly damage unprotected outdoor\nplumbing.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The growing season officially ends on October\n31, after which no further frost or freeze headlines will be\nissued.",
